   "t": 1791260555.614264,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "My trigger fired and the stop was executed. This is a single-feature specification (feature 36, negative sign) with in-sample Sharpe 1.6068. Given this is the result of the init move alone (the \"best single feature\" search over 80 candidates \u2014 presumably 40 features \u00d7 2 signs), this Sharpe already comfortably clears my bar of 1.2.\n\nA single-feature spec picked as literally the best of 80 sign/feature combinations in-sample is likely to be overstated out-of-sample (selection bias from choosing the best of many). I should temper my OOS prediction accordingly rather than take the in-sample number at face value."
